                            <h4>Babusar Top</h4>

                            <div class="contact">
                                <p>
                                    The Babusar Top, also known as Babusar Pass, is located in the
                                    Kaghan Valley's northwestern corner. It connects the provinces
                                    of Khyber Pakhtunkhwa and Gilgit Baltistan. Babusar Top is the
                                    highest point in Pakistan that is easily accessible by car or
                                    jeep. During the summer, the location provides a captivating
                                    and stunning view. However, keep in mind that the place is
                                    high and freezing upwards. The Babusar Pass, at 4,173 meters
                                    above sea level, is the highest point in the Himalayas. It is
                                    also the end of the Naran Kaghan Region.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

